{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774740,"nonce":"xz2sVhjGdq3cK00onF8qoPs4MEs=","title":"fix(auth): make ADR-0049 OAuth login deployable and strict enough for a real OIDC issuer","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #84 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `fix/oauth-hardening-and-chart` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-25T19:50:08Z · Merged: 2026-07-25T20:01:37Z\n\nCloses four git-bug tickets from an audit prompted by a simple question: *does\nScarab need an OIDC or Dex integration?* It does not — `oauth.rs` is already a\ngeneric OAuth/OIDC relying party. But the chart couldn't configure it, and the\nadapter wasn't strict enough to safely trust a real OIDC issuer.\n\n\n`grep -ri oauth deploy/helm/` returned nothing. The configmap only ever set\n`SCARAB_DEV_INSECURE`, never the `SCARAB_OAUTH_*` five-tuple `config.rs:532`\nrequires. A chart-deployed Scarab had two reachable states: boot **dev-insecure**\n(every caller a synthetic Owner) or **refuse to boot**\n(`ConfigError::NoAuthenticator`). ADR-0049 authn — sessions, CSRF, scoped RBAC —\nwas implemented but unreachable through the distribution chart.\n\nAdds `scarab.oauth.*` plus `secrets.oauthClientSecret.{name,key}`, mirroring the\nexisting `githubAppPemSecret` pattern so the client secret arrives via\n`secretKeyRef` and never sits in `values.yaml`. A `scarab.validateAuth` helper\nrefuses three contradictory configs at render time: a partial provider (naming the\nmissing keys), oauth with no reachable client secret, and `devInsecure` alongside\noauth. \"No authenticator at all\" stays the chart default and the *server's*\nrefusal to own — failing it at render time would break `helm lint`.\n\n\nThe adapter took `access_token` and called userinfo, ignoring `id_token`\nentirely: no signature check, no `iss`/`aud`/`exp`, no nonce. Fine for GitHub\n(plain OAuth2, no id_token); wrong for a real OIDC issuer, where the id_token\n*is* the authenticated assertion and userinfo is merely a bearer-authorized\nlookup.\n\nWith the new optional `SCARAB_OAUTH_ISSUER` set, the id_token is verified RS256\nagainst that issuer's discovery JWKS (kid-cached, refetched on miss) and its\nclaims are authoritative. **A present-but-invalid id_token fails the login — it\nnever falls back to userinfo.** Providers returning no id_token are unchanged.\n\n\n`authorize_redirect` sent no `code_challenge`. A new `LoginFlow` carries state +\nverifier + nonce in the one existing opaque `HttpOnly` cookie; the redirect sends\n`code_challenge_method=S256` and the callback replays the verifier. The\n`Authenticator` port signature is **unchanged**, so `POST /v1/auth/login`\n(API/CLI) still works and only forwards a verifier when the client sends one.\n\n\nOwner matching keyed on the subject, which for Dex/Keycloak/Google is an opaque\nper-client id — so bootstrapping the first admin meant discovering and pasting a\nUUID before anyone could administer anything. An owner entry now also matches a\n**verified** email claim. Unverified email never grants Owner; `sub` remains the\nstored Principal identity.\n\n\n- `SCARAB_OAUTH_ISSUER` is **optional**; unset preserves today's behaviour\n  exactly. Setting it *alone* is a `PartialOAuth` boot refusal, keeping\n  all-five-or-none coherent — and the chart's `oauthConfigured` predicate had to\n  learn about it, or issuer-only silently rendered no oauth env at all.\n- One new dependency: `sha2` (workspace) for the S256 challenge.\n- ADR-0049 gets an amendment section; `Status` untouched.\n- All chart keys default empty, so **existing installs render unchanged**.\n\n\n`cargo check --workspace` clean. **`just test` → 648 passed, 21 skipped**,\nincluding 10 new `oauth_flow` tests covering the forged/wrong-aud/wrong-iss/\nexpired id_token rejections, the no-fallback guarantee, PKCE verifier\nround-trip, the API path without a verifier, and verified-vs-unverified email\nowner matching.\n\n`helm lint` → 0 failed. `helm template` across the permutations that matter:\ndefaults, full oauth, oauth+issuer (emits `SCARAB_OAUTH_ISSUER`), oauth without\nissuer (correctly omits it), issuer-alone (fails with the four missing keys\nnamed), existingSecret-only, devInsecure-only, and the three invalid configs each\nfailing with their intended message.\n\n`just pr-gate 84` has **not** been run — that's the pre-merge gate for this repo.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}